      "body": "Hi, before opening any PR (CONTRIBUTING says to open an issue when unsure), two small spec/consistency findings in the engineering-team skills:\n\n1. `engineering-team/skills/epic-design/SKILL.md` lines 245-247 point to `assets/hero-section.html`, `assets/hero-section.css` and `assets/hero-section.js` (\"Full boilerplate / Full CSS system / Full JS engine\"), but the skill directory only contains `SKILL.md`, `references/` and `scripts/`; there is no `assets/` folder and no `hero-section.*` file anywhere in the repo. An agent following the pointers will look for files that do not exist.\n2. `engineering-team/playwright-pro/skills/pw/SKILL.md` has `name: \"playwright-pro\"` but its parent folder is `pw`. The Agent Skills spec (https://agentskills.io/specification) says the `name` field \"Must match the parent directory name.\"\n\nWhich fix do you prefer?\n- For 1: (a) add the three asset files, or (b) remove the three pointer lines (or point them at the inline snippet above them).\n- For 2: (a) rename the frontmatter `name` to `pw`, or (b) rename the folder (e.g. `skills/playwright-pro/`), or (c) keep it as an intentional exception.\n\nHappy to open a PR for whichever you choose.\n\nFound with the audit script of skill-skill: https://github.com/jack-reson8/skill-skill\n",
